# E2E data dirs: never commit test data. Every one holds a generated api_key.
#
# NOT "and seeded provider credentials": scripts/seed_e2e_data.py writes an
# api_key and no password (see its own docstring). ci.yml rests the safety of
# uploading test-results/ on that same fact, so the two statements have to
# agree -- and the direction of the error mattered, because the version that
# over-claimed was the one a reader would have used to argue the artefact
# upload was unsafe.
#
# Matches ANY .e2e-* name, not `.e2e-*data/`. That narrower glob required the
# name to END in "data", which is why `.e2e-data-mobile` and `.e2e-data-a11y`
# needed hand-written entries, and why `make check-secrets` was red on master
# until T1.7. Removing those two entries in favour of the narrow glob (as an
# earlier commit on this branch did) un-ignored two directories that still
# exist on any machine which ran the suite before T1.7, each holding a live
# key. A pattern that covers the class cannot regress that way.
.e2e-*
.claude/worktrees/
